     "checked_on": "2026-10-08"
    }
   ],
   "notes": "Built (lane ENTAPI-L16E, T-717): a customer_host surface (LiteLLM is third-party software the customer deploys in front of Poolside inference, on its own domain; the connection declares the tuple, ledger VCONN-HOST-1). Driver internal/vendorapi/poolside LiteLLM: GET /user/daily/activity with start_date and end_date (UTC dates, at most one day per run), page 1, page_size 1000; user_id, api_key, model and timezone are never sent. Paging is over the gateway's daily spend rows, not dates, so a split day would land partial: an answer with has_more or total_pages above one is refused as schema drift. Tool attribution: gateway traffic is any client's, so every row lands as an UNATTRIBUTED org-level fact under the reserved value gateway:litellm (vendorapi.GatewayTool), never the poolside tool; nothing on a spend, budget, alert or enforcement path reads it. Facts per (UTC day, model): cost (usd, the documented float converted to micro-dollars with a bounded exponent), input, output tokens and requests, plus cache read and write tokens and successful and failed requests when present (absent is never zero). The api_keys breakdown (hashed keys with alias, team, user and e-mail) and every other breakdown are never decoded: closed DTO, secret class may_return_secret kept. The documented example shows flat model entries; the endpoint's source nests them under metrics, which the driver follows (a flat entry is drift). [BETA] per the endpoint's own docstring. Synthetic only, no vendor response observed: assumption_tested.",
   "derivation": {
    "reach_rule": "override: LiteLLM admin API on the customer deployment",
    "build_rule": "lane ENTAPI-L16E: driver internal/vendorapi/poolside LiteLLM, synthetic gate passed",
    "source_rule": "literal_url",
    "auth_rule": "plane: LiteLLM proxy key auth: Authorization: Bearer <key> (cost_tracking.md examples)"
   },
   "status": "synthetic, awaiting live validation",
   "customer_host": true
